//
// Let the power daemon take the lid switch off logind.
//
// PWR-R4 wants Arlen to decide what a closing lid means, because logind cannot:
// it has no way to skip the suspend just because an external display is attached,
// so a docked laptop sleeps when you shut it. The mechanism is a BLOCK inhibitor
// on `handle-lid-switch`, which makes logind defer, and it has never once been
// granted - the 12 Aug boot logged `could not inhibit logind lid handling`, and
// the takeover has been dead on every image since it was written.
//
// The reason is not the lid and not the hardware. logind's default policy for
// inhibit-handle-lid-switch is `allow_active=yes` and `allow_any=no`, and
// `allow_any` is the row for a subject in no session at all. `arlen-powerd` is a
// user unit, so it lives in user@.service, and a process there has no session:
// `sd_pid_get_session` fails for it by design, which is what makes user services
// survive logout. Active is therefore unreachable for it however it is started,
// and the answer is `no` every time.
//
// So this grants the one action to the desktop user explicitly. It is a smaller
// widening than it looks: the same user's session processes are already allowed
// the identical action by `allow_active=yes`, so all this does is extend to their
// user units what their session already has. The worst it can be abused for is a
// laptop that does not sleep on close, which is a nuisance and not a privilege -
// and every process it applies to is already running as the person the machine
// belongs to.
//
// Scoped by name rather than uid deliberately, matching ARLEN_OWNER_USER: the
// desktop uid is whatever useradd picked, and a hardcoded 1000 would silently
// grant nothing on a machine that numbered its first user differently.
//
// Nothing reads this file unless polkitd is installed, which until 12 Aug it was
// not. See the polkitd entry in mkosi.conf for that half.
polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id == "org.freedesktop.login1.inhibit-handle-lid-switch" &&
        subject.user == "arlen") {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
});
